{
  "requirement": {
    "id": "I2-005",
    "source": "UR I2 Structural Requirements for Polar Class Ships",
    "clause": "I2.2.5",
    "text": "I2.2.5 The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where\n         the shell is inclined 7° from horizontal."
  },
  "source_documents": [
    {
      "file": "data/requirements/IACS_I2_full.txt",
      "sha256": "7ad8d57459782b70809da479380584a57cf259c66d9ff286811c0248b02732d2",
      "text": "                                                                                                           I2\n\n\n\nI2          Structural Requirements for Polar Class Ships\n(August\n(cont)\n2006)       I2.1 General\n(Rev.1\nJan 2007)   I2.1.1 Application*\n(Corr.1\nOct 2007)   This UR applies to Polar Class ships according to UR I1.\n(Rev.2\nNov 2010)   I2.1.2 Definitions\n(Rev.3\nApr 2016)   I2.1.2.1 The length LUI is the distance, in m, measured horizontally from the fore side of the\n(Rev.4      stem at the intersection with the upper ice waterline (UIWL) to the after side of the rudder\nDec 2019)   post, or the centre of the rudder stock if there is no rudder post. LUI is not to be less than\n            96%, and need not be greater than 97%, of the extreme length of the upper ice waterline\n            (UIWL) measured horizontally from the fore side of the stem. In ships with unusual stern and\n            bow arrangement the length LUI will be specially considered.\n\n",
      "authority": "User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified",
      "selection": {
        "start": 0,
        "end": 970,
        "section_ids": [
          "PREAMBLE"
        ],
        "sha256": "be8937e4ee2c8851545f9b8f4b039f46e25a3a7822426c4083a778c79ab471ab"
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "data/requirements/IACS_I2_full.txt",
      "sha256": "7ad8d57459782b70809da479380584a57cf259c66d9ff286811c0248b02732d2",
      "text": "            I2.2 Hull areas\n\n",
      "authority": "User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified",
      "selection": {
        "start": 1304,
        "end": 1333,
